course: dictionary
lesson: 2219
title: Courtesy and polite words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Courtesy means polite, kind and respectful behaviour towards other people. Saying please and thank you, holding a door and waiting your turn are all courtesy. Look at the example: «The traveller greets the Rat with a gesture of courtesy that had something foreign about it.» A gesture is a small movement, such as a nod or a bow, so the traveller shows politeness with a small action.
explain: Courtesy can also mean one polite act or remark, and that is called a courtesy. In the same sentences, the Rat lets the traveller rest «unquestioned», so the Rat does not ask him to explain himself. The context shows that courtesy is about how people treat each other.
explain: The word also appears in phrases. A courtesy bus or courtesy car is given free as a polite service, so you do not pay for it. «Courtesy of» means given or made possible by someone. Common courtesy means the basic politeness everyone is expected to show. Use the words around the word to choose the right meaning.
fact: Courtesy means polite, kind and respectful behaviour.
fact: A courtesy is a polite act or remark, such as saying «thank you».
fact: A «courtesy bus» or «courtesy car» is free, given as a polite service.
fact: «Courtesy of» means given or made possible by someone.
fact: «Common courtesy» means the basic politeness people expect from each other.
exercise: «The traveller greets the Rat with a gesture of courtesy.» What does courtesy mean here? | *Polite, respectful behaviour | Rudeness and noise | Being very tired | A loud shout
exercise: Saying please and thank you is an example of what? | Being late | *Courtesy | A long walk | A bus timetable
exercise: A «courtesy bus» at the airport is what? | Broken down | *Free, given as a polite service | Only for children | Very expensive
test: In «Photo courtesy of the museum», what does courtesy of mean? | Paid for by the visitor | *Made possible by the museum | Lost in the museum | Stolen from the museum
test: Which word is the best synonym for courtesy? | *Politeness | Rudeness | Anger | Silence
exam: Which is a courtesy, meaning a polite act or remark? | *Saying «Excuse me» when you pass someone | Losing your coat | Sitting in silence | Running out of the room
